.TH CHANGELOG-RELEASE 8 "July 2026" "changelog 1.0.0" "System Administration Commands"
.SH NAME
changelog release \- generate release changelog entries from accumulated fragments
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B changelog release
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBrelease\fR command aggregates all fragment files into a structured release changelog. It processes fragments in the configured directory, applies sorting and filtering rules, generates version entries with proper formatting, and archives processed fragments according to configuration settings.

This is the primary workflow command for producing release notes. Fragments accumulate over time as developers add them via \fBchangelog add\fR, then \fBrelease\fR consolidates them into a coherent changelog entry for each version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help message and exit.

.TP
.B Required:
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR=\fIVERSION\fR
Release version in semver format (e.g., "v1.0.0", "2.3.1"). Must match the project's configured version pattern.

.TP
.B Optional:
.TP
\fB\-\-date\fR=\fIYYYY\-MM\-DD\fR
Release date. Defaults to today if not specified. Used for chronological ordering and metadata.

.TP
\fB\-\-codename\fR=\fICODENAME\fR
Human-readable codename for the release (e.g., "Stardust", "Nebula"). Displayed in changelog headers when configured.

.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-dir\fR=\fIPATH\fR
Changelog base directory containing fragments/. Defaults to current directory's \fIchangelogs/\fR subdirectory.

.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-notes-dir\fR=\fIDIR\fR
Additional fragment directories to merge into the release output. Can be specified multiple times for multiple notes directories. Useful for organizing fragments by subsystem or team.

.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR=\fIFILE\fR
Output file path for the generated changelog entry. Defaults to "CHANGELOG.md" in the current directory. Can be absolute or relative paths.

.TP
\fB\-\-reload\-plugins\fR
Force reload of plugin cache during release generation. Useful when plugins have been added/removed since last release.

.TP
\fB\-\-refresh\fR
Update existing entries from fragments and refresh plugin descriptions. Combines fragment processing with metadata updates.

.TP
\fB\-\-refresh\-plugins\fR=\fIMODE\fR
Specify how to handle plugin description updates:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fIallow\-removal\fR (default) \- Allow plugins to be removed from changelog if no longer present
.IP \(bu 2
\fIprevent\-removal\fR \- Keep all previously documented plugins even if source files changed
.RE

.TP
\fB\-\-refresh\-fragments\fR=\fIMODE\fR
Control which fragments to include in refresh:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fIwithout\-archives\fR (default) \- Only process non-archived fragments
.IP \(bu 2
\fIwith\-archives\fR \- Include archived/processed fragments for full regeneration
.RE

.TP
\fB\-\-collection\-namespace\fR=\fINAMESPACE\fR
Override the collection namespace for Ansible-style projects. Used when generating plugin documentation references.

.TP
\fB\-\-collection\-name\fR=\fINAME\fR
Override the collection name. Combined with \fB\-\-collection\-namespace\fR for fully qualified plugin paths.

.TP
\fB\-\-collection\-flatmap\fR
Enable flat mapping of collections, using short plugin names instead of fully qualified names in output.

.TP
\fB\-\-is\-collection\fR=\fIBOOL\fR
Override whether this is a collection project (true/false/yes/no). Affects how fragments are processed and output formatting.

.TP
\fB\-\-update\-existing\fR
If a release entry already exists for this version, update its date/codename instead of erroring out. Useful for correcting metadata on existing releases.

.TP
\fB\-\-cumulative\-release\fR
Include all plugins/modules added since the previous release or ancestor version. Generates comprehensive "what's new" sections.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-semantic\-versioning\fR
Disable semantic versioning enforcement for this release. Allows non-semver version strings (e.g., "latest", "nightly").
.SH FRAGMENT PROCESSING
.PP
During release generation, the tool:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Reads all fragment files from the main directory and any notes directories
.IP \(bu 2
Validates each fragment against configured rules (see \fBchangelog-lint(8)\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
Groups fragments by category and version
.IP \(bu 2
Applies sorting rules based on category priority and date
.IP \(bu 3
Generates markdown output with proper headers, sections, and formatting
.IP \(bu 4
Archives processed fragments according to \fBkeep_fragments\fR configuration
.RE

.TP
.B Category Priority (rendering order):
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
1. Breaking Changes / Porting Guide
.IP \(bu 2
2. Major Changes
.IP \(bu 2
3. Deprecated Features
.IP \(bu 2
4. Removed Features
.IP \(bu 2
5. Bugfixes
.IP \(bu 2
6. Security Fixes
.IP \(bu 2
7. Minor Changes
.IP \(bu 2
8. Known Issues
.RE

.TP
.B Archiving Behavior:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Fragments are moved to \fI.changes/archives/\fR after processing (default)
.IP \(bu 2
Set \fBkeep_fragments: true\fR in config.yaml to retain fragments after release
.IP \(bu 2
Archive directory can be customized via \fBarchive_path_template\fR in configuration
.RE
.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
.PP
Generated changelog entries follow this structure:
.nf
    ## [v1.0.0] - 2026-07-29

    ### Breaking Changes / Porting Guide
    * **PG-001**: Fixed crash when processing large files.

    ### Bugfixes
    * **IMP-456**: Added support for parallel processing.

    ### Minor Changes
    * **DOC-123**: Documentation updates.
.fi

.TP
.B Version Headers:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Format: \fI## [vX.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD\fR (or codename if specified)
.IP \(bu 2
Includes semver version with 'v' prefix and release date
.RE

.TP
.B Section Headers:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Format: \fI### <Category Name>\fR matching configured section titles
.IP \(bu 2
Categories render in priority order as listed above
.RE

.TP
.B Fragment Entries:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Format: \fI* **<issue>**: <text>\fR for simple entries
.IP \(bu 2
Multi-line content wrapped with proper indentation
.IP \(bu 2
Code blocks preserved with syntax highlighting if configured
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Basic release generation:
.nf
    changelog release --version v1.0.0
.fi

.TP
Release with custom date and codename:
.nf
    changelog release \\
        --version v2.1.0 \\
        --date 2026-08-15 \\
        --codename "Nebula" \\
        --output releases/v2.1.0.md
.fi

.TP
Release with multiple notes directories:
.nf
    changelog release \\
        --version v3.0.0 \\
        -n changelogs/fragments/core \\
        -n changelogs/fragments/plugins \\
        -n changelogs/notes/community
.fi

.TP
Release with plugin refresh and cumulative mode:
.nf
    changelog release \\
        --version v1.5.0 \\
        --refresh \\
        --refresh-plugins allow-removal \\
        --cumulative-release \\
        --collection-namespace myorg.myplugin
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO
